    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d807">

                <pb facs="1273" n="1259" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1259"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 E.W./10–2044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Representative on the Advisory Council for
                        Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-20T15:00:00+01:00">October 20, 1944—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>564. My 549, October 18, midnight and Department’s 307, October 18, 6 p.m. At
                    today’s meeting the ACI agreed in principle to recommend <pb facs="1274"
                        n="1260" xml:id="pg1260"/> to the respective governments represented on the
                    Council that with reference to the German atrocities in Northern Italy a
                    statement be issued by the governments warning the Germans.</p>
                <p>The text of the recommendation will be drafted shortly and submitted to all
                    representatives for approval. Pending approval of this text the Council is
                    requesting complete lists of all reported atrocities from both the Italian
                    Government, through the ACC, and AFHQ, these lists will be added as an annex to
                    the above mentioned recommendation at the time of its transmission to the
                    respective governments.</p>
                <p>It appears from today’s discussion on this subject that both the Greek and
                    Yugoslav representatives in transmitting the Council’s recommendation to their
                    respective governments will add their own observations and comments thereon with
                    special reference to atrocities on their respective territories.<anchor n="50"
                        xml:id="d807-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d807-f1" n="50" xml:id="d807-f1-content">
                <p>On November 17, 1944, the Advisory Council for Italy agreed to postpone
                    consideration of the problem of German atrocities in Northern Italy until
                    further communication from the Italian Government.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
